diff --git a/docs/architecture.md b/docs/architecture.md
index 48bb292..324ada6 100644
--- a/docs/architecture.md
+++ b/docs/architecture.md
@@ -215,6 +215,11 @@ lines and common natural-language requests for help, review, linearization, quit
 one or more user agents. Multi-agent launch requests dispatch `new [prompt...]` once per requested
 agent through the same controller paths used by command-mode input.
 
+The controller tracks the most recently selected agent session. `execute_command_line` treats a
+trimmed line that starts with `/` followed by a non-whitespace character as a selected-agent command
+when a selected session exists, and routes that text through `send_message` instead of the
+`command-agent` transcript. Slash followed by whitespace remains ordinary Work Leaf command input.
+
 Frontend code should use these methods:
 
 - `WorkLeafController::new` to wrap a `CommandChat<B>`.
@@ -287,7 +292,9 @@ Bracketed-paste newlines and Shift+Enter are chat prompt line breaks. A plain En
 buffered chat text.
 When an agent chat is selected in command mode, `/` focuses the chat, seeds the chat buffer with
 `/`, and enters insert mode so `/status`-style input submits through the same selected-agent chat
-path.
+path. Prompt-mode command lines such as `/status` also submit to the selected agent. If the command
+row is selected, the same prompt text stays on the Work Leaf command surface and renders the unknown
+command diagnostic there.
 
 Command mode supports terminal-local visual selection in both panes. `v` starts character selection,
 `V` starts line selection, and Ctrl-V starts block selection from the focused pane row or chat cursor.
